Looking at the artifact, the core bug is that the CSRF token is captured once during `login()` and then reused across all three iterations of the `repeat(3)` loop. When the session is renewed (expiry mode), the fresh CSRF returned by `/v2/session/renew` is saved to `staleCsrf` instead of `csrf`, so subsequent iterations keep sending the stale token.

The fix: every place that captures a fresh CSRF from a renewal (or any authenticated response) must write it back to `csrf`, and the renewal must happen at the correct scope — i.e., per-iteration, not once before the loop. Also the `login()` must run inside the loop so each iteration starts fresh, and the renewal must update `csrf` so the next iteration uses the rotated token.

Here is the corrected simulation:

